From 6111345137850102322e65ed9f397a9d91e125c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:38:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/27] Tensor parallelism across CUDA processes: bootstrap,
 NCCL, mailbox and RoCE collectives, plan link, fail-fast.

zig/src/fabric/tp brings a rank up from TF_TP_WORLD, TF_TP_RANK, TF_TP_MASTER and TF_TP_PORT, agrees the settings
digest over every rank, and gives a family all-gather, all-reduce and broadcast over NCCL (TF_COMM_BACKEND=nccl,
the default), a pinned host mailbox for ranks on one host, or RoCE verbs between two hosts (TF_TP_ROCE_*), with an
NCCL fallback when RoCE setup fails. Rank 0 sends each round's plan to the others over its own link (TF_TP_PLAN_*).
A failure or a vanished rank ends every rank shortly after (TF_TP_FAILFAST, TF_TP_FAILFAST_GRACE_S).
No family uses it yet. zig build test-tp runs the host tests; zig build tf-tp-test builds the two-GPU runner
(-Dtp-nvcc= or -Dtp-fatbin= for the mailbox kernel). The RoCE all-gather adapts b12x's RoCEnante protocol.

(cherry picked from commit 0824e393b27ba8ebce8663762686d8bb2730f3da)
